<title>GREECE: Bank of Greece drains 14-day funds at 11.87 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Greece drains 14-day funds at 11.87 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Greece drained 200 billion drachmas of 14-day funds at a weighted average interest rate of 11.87 percent, it said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Payment date is March 26 and maturity value date April 9.</p>
<p>Accepted bids for the 14-day depo tender ranged from 11.80 to 11.88 percent, the central bank said.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
